course: dictionary
lesson: 15166
title: Scrambled: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Scrambled is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «For breakfast, Mum made scrambled eggs on toast.» Here the eggs were beaten and cooked in a pan, so scrambled means cooked until soft, not mixed up.
explain: «The letters on the card were scrambled, so I could not read the word.» The clue is could not read. Scrambled means mixed up so it makes no sense. Word puzzles often use scrambled words, which you must unscramble to find the real word.
explain: «We scrambled up the muddy hill to reach the top.» Here scrambled is a verb. We climbed quickly and awkwardly, using our hands and feet. «My brain is scrambled after that long quiz» is informal and means confused. Check the clues each time, then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Scrambled» can describe eggs cooked and stirred in a pan, or letters mixed up so they cannot be read.
fact: «Scrambled» can also mean climbed quickly and awkwardly, as in «scrambled up the hill».
fact: «Scrambled» can mean confused, as in «My brain is scrambled», and it is an informal way to say it.
exercise: «Dad made scrambled eggs for breakfast.» What are scrambled eggs? | *Eggs beaten and cooked in a pan while being stirred | Eggs still in their shells | Eggs thrown at the wall | Eggs painted in bright colours
exercise: «The letters were scrambled, so the word was impossible to read.» What does scrambled mean here? | Read out loud very clearly | Neatly written in rows | Painted in gold | *Mixed up so it makes no sense
exercise: «We scrambled up the rocks to the cave.» What kind of word is scrambled in this sentence? | An adjective, a word that describes a thing | A noun, the name of a thing | *A verb, an action word | A full stop
test: «The signal was scrambled, so the spies could not read the message.» What does scrambled mean here? | Sent by post | *Coded so outsiders cannot read it | Loud and clear | Written in pencil
test: Tom says, «My brain is scrambled» after the quiz. What does he mean? | He is very hungry | *He feels confused | His head is very clean | He has lots of bright new ideas
exam: Which sentence uses scrambled to mean confused? | «The letters were scrambled on the card.» | «We scrambled up the hill to see the view.» | *«My brain feels scrambled after that long quiz.» | «The eggs were scrambled in the pan.»
